<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
   <teiHeader>
      <fileDesc>
         <titleStmt>
            <title>Mary Behrend's Calendar Letters</title>
         </titleStmt>
         <publicationStmt>
            <p>Published by Dr. B on the newtFire website</p>
         </publicationStmt>
         <sourceDesc>
            <p>A series of handwritten calendar entries done by Mary Behrend in the year 1909</p>
         </sourceDesc>
      </fileDesc>
   </teiHeader>
   <text>
      <group>
         <text>
            <front>
               <dateline>
                  <date when="1909-01-30">JANUARY 30, 1909. SATURDAY</date>
               </dateline>
            </front>
            <body>
               <p>
                  <lb/>E.R.B.
                  <quote>
                     <lb/>"That damned old clock
                     <lb/><space quantity="7" unit="char"/> gives me a ?
                     <lb/>Back <unclear>seeing</unclear> where it's dark
                     <lb/><emph><unclear>It</unclear> likes</emph> its fun, but I've <unclear>begun</unclear>
                     <lb/><space quantity="3" unit="char"/>To tire of thee <unclear>dark</unclear>
                  </quote>
               </p>
            </body>
         </text>
         <text>
            <front>
               <dateline>
                  <date when="1909-02-16">FEBRUARY 16, 1909. TUESDAY</date>
               </dateline>
            </front>
            <body>
               <p>
                  <lb/>Mr. Behrend finds a
                  <lb/><space quantity="1" unit="char"/>bed bug!
                  <lb/><hi rend="red-ink">I <unclear>wonder</unclear> if you have found many lately!</hi>
               </p>
            </body>
         </text>
         <text>
            <front>
               <dateline>
                  <date when="1909-02-17">FEBRUARY 17, 1909. WEDNESDAY</date>
               </dateline>
            </front>
            <body>
               <p>
                  <lb/>Each morning <emph>very</emph> early
                  <lb/>When all is dark &amp; still
                  <lb/>Ernst <unclear>goes in</unclear> <unclear>inky blackness</unclear>
                  <lb/>To <unclear>work</unclear> at Hammermill
                  <lb/>I really think he's very good
                  <lb/>To get up when it's dark
                  <lb/>For this he <emph>says</emph> he doesn't mind
                  <lb/>He can't <unclear>duck</unclear> a <emph>lark</emph>!
                  <lb/><hi rend="red-ink">Poor thing! is it still dark when you arise?</hi>
               </p>
            </body>
         </text>
      </group>
   </text>
</TEI>
